---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
---

<PageLayout
  title="About — Harrison Mohr"
  description="Applied AI engineer building production AI agent systems. From audio production to ML engineering."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-8 sm:gap-12 mb-12">
      <div class="shrink-0">
        <img
          src="/images/headshot.png"
          alt="Harrison Mohr"
          class="w-36 h-36 rounded-full object-cover"
          width="144"
          height="144"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-1">Harrison Mohr</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-muted mb-4">Applied AI Engineer</p>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-muted">
          <a
            href="https://github.com/jackharrisonmohr"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="hover:text-accent transition-colors"
          >
            GitHub
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jack-harrison-m-4280b9a5/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="hover:text-accent transition-colors"
          >
            LinkedIn
          </a>
          <a
            href="mailto:jackharrisonmohr@gmail.com"
            class="hover:text-accent transition-colors"
          >
            jackharrisonmohr@gmail.com
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert prose-lg max-w-none">
      <p>
        I'm the founding engineer at <a href="https://maketimeflow.com">MakeTimeFlow</a>,
        building production AI agent systems: voice-enabled coaching, LLM
        orchestration, and real-time integrations. I drive the full product
        lifecycle in close collaboration with the CEO, from customer research
        and product strategy through architecture and deployment. My current
        work spans AI agent development (Claude API, ElevenLabs real-time voice),
        backend system design, and building AI-native development workflows for
        the engineering team itself.
      </p>

      <p>
        Previously, I led engineering on two NSF-funded ML platforms ($1.2M+
        combined) at the University of Houston, owning the full AWS stack and
        bridging the gap between ML model outputs and user-facing applications.
        One of those platforms supported emergency food distribution logistics
        for the Houston Food Bank. Before that, I built deep learning training
        pipelines for medical imaging research at UChicago's Department of
        Radiology, where I led a small team developing segmentation models for
        renal cell carcinoma detection and built an automated video generation
        pipeline that let the team visually diagnose model failure modes across
        temporal CT sequences.
      </p>

      <p>
        My path into engineering wasn't conventional. I studied audio design and
        production at Columbia College Chicago, where I wrote and produced music
        that's since accumulated over two million views on YouTube. That
        background gave me an obsession with signal quality, careful listening,
        and building things that work in the real world. Those instincts
        transferred directly when I pivoted to computer science and earned my
        M.A.S. at Illinois Institute of Technology.
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm genuinely energized by this moment in AI. The power of these systems
        is growing fast, and how we build them matters as much as what we build.
        I care about building systems that hold up under real-world pressure, and
        I think the best engineering happens when technical rigor meets curiosity
        and a real connection to the people using the thing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
